CORE dfcc-only
main.c
--dfcc main --enforce-contract my_log
^\[my_log\.assigns\.\d+\] line 9 Check that g is assignable: SUCCESS$
^\[my_log\.assertion\.1\] line 10 body is reachable: FAILURE$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^file main.c line 3: variadic arguments are not passed to function 'my_log' when checking its contract$
--
--
The harness and the wrapper of a variadic function under contract have to pass
the write set where the wrapper and the wrapped function, respectively, have
their write set parameter. Otherwise n binds to the write set, the requires
clause cannot hold, and the body of my_log is unreachable. As the variadic
arguments are not passed on to the wrapped function, DFCC warns.
